    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5385" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμοιβ-ᾰδίς</span></b> , Adv., (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμοιβή</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>by turns, alternately,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἄλλοθεν ἄλλος</span> one after
			another, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				1.34
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἀνέρος ἀνὴρ ἑζόμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					4.199
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Nonn.
				<u>D.</u>
				24.227
			</span></i>:—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμοιβ-αδόν</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
				Parm.
				1.19
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				2.1226
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ti.Locr.
				68e
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Them.
				<u>Or.</u>
				17.215b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Agath.
				2.21
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>in turn, again,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Epigr.Gr.
				998.9
			</span></i>.</div>
